      "text_raw": "The input resistance R is\nIN\nnow the open-loop input\nresistance R multiplied\nINOL\nby the loop gain LG.\nThe open-loop input\nresistance R is simply\nINOL\nthe sum of the large input\nresistor R and the feed-\nNP\nback resistors in parallel.\nOutput resistance R is\nO\nsmall and therefore negligi-\nble with respect to the\nothers.\nThis input resistance\nR is about infinity for a\nINOL\nMOST amplifier but not for\na bipolar one. Application of series feedback will make the closed-loop input resistance R near\nIN\ninfinity for a bipolar amplifier.\nNote that for the calculation of the open-loop input resistance, the effect of the feedback must\nbe eliminated. This is easily done by setting the gain A to zero.\n0",
      "text": "The input resistance R is IN now the open-loop input resistance R multiplied INOL by the loop gain LG. The open-loop input resistance R is simply INOL the sum of the large input resistor R and the feed- NP back resistors in parallel. Output resistance R is O small and therefore negligible with respect to the others. This input resistance R is about infinity for a INOL MOST amplifier but not for a bipolar one. Application of series feedback will make the closed-loop input resistance R near IN infinity for a bipolar amplifier. Note that for the calculation of the open-loop input resistance, the effect of the feedback must be eliminated. This is easily done by setting the gain A to zero. 0"
    }
